# hive.env.example — every figure the Scry Hive launch needs, in one place.
#
#   cp hive.env.example hive.env      # hive.env IS gitignored (`*.env`).
#                                     # Put the key in the environment, never here.
#   set -a; . ./hive.env; set +a
#   forge script script/DeploySeat.s.sol --rpc-url $RPC            # DRY RUN FIRST
#
# The order these are used in is docs/launch/HIVE-LAUNCH.md. This file is the
# figures; that file is the ceremony, and it says which steps cannot be undone.
#
# ⚠ PRIVATE_KEY IS NOT IN THIS FILE AND MUST NOT BE ADDED TO IT. The deploy
#   scripts read it from the environment. A key in a file next to a template
#   named .example is exactly the habit .gitignore's secret block exists to
#   catch, and the catch is second-line — it is not a plan.
#
# LEGEND, and it is the only thing here that really matters:
#
#   [WELDED]  immutable at construction. No setter exists. Wrong = redeploy.
#   [SETTER]  changeable later, cheaply.
#   [TIMELOCK] changeable later, after 3 days.
#
# Anything still marked <UNSPOKEN> has no operator sentence in docs/SENTENCES.md
# and is left BLANK on purpose — a figure copied out of a template is exactly how
# a ladder nobody chose got welded into a constructor argument once already (see
# DeploySeat.s.sol's header). Every figure carrying a value here has a sentence.
#
# ⚠ A SPOKEN FIGURE IS NOT A FROZEN ONE WHERE IT DEPENDS ON THE TAPE. The cistern
# knobs were sized against SCRY at $0.00001782 on 2026-08-12; the SENTENCE is the
# cadence they were chosen to produce, not the integer. Re-run
# `python3 meter/cistern_sizing.py` before broadcasting and check the integer
# still buys that cadence. Same for the reserve window, which is "60 days from
# DEPLOY" and therefore a different timestamp every day you wait.

# ── the chain ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# ⚠ THIS READ `rpc.robinhoodchain.com` UNTIL 2026-08-13, AND THAT HOST DOES NOT
#   EXIST — it fails in TLS with "UnrecognisedName", before any JSON-RPC. The
#   very first command in this file's own header would have failed on it. The
#   public endpoint is the one meter/holder_snapshot.py has always defaulted to;
#   `cast chain-id --rpc-url $RPC` answers 4663 on it.
RPC=https://rpc.mainnet.chain.robinhood.com
# ⚠ FOR THE BROADCAST, PREFER A KEYED PROVIDER. The public endpoint 403s from
#   this box for some methods (meter/rh_tools.py §218) and is rate-limited for
#   everyone. RUNBOOK.md §209:
#     RPC="$(printf '%s' "$SCRY_RH_RPC_POOL" | cut -d, -f1)"   # from keys.env
# PRIVATE_KEY — export it in your shell. Not here. See above.

# ── ScrySeat: welded at construction ─────────────────────────────────────────
SEAT_NAME="Scry Hive"
SEAT_SYMBOL=HIVE
SEAT_SCRY=0xDa2a4b23459e9ca88183e990802be644AcA7C4B0
SEAT_SPLITTER=0xcB8f6Ec8A7A2a7d55E7e5dD9B2c5CcC4707e7996

SEAT_SUPPLY=8192                # [WELDED] operator, 2026-08-08
SEAT_TREASURY_CAP=100           # [WELDED] operator, 2026-08-08
SEAT_BURN_BPS=5000              # [WELDED] operator — half of every activation to 0xdEaD
SEAT_ROYALTY_BPS=500            # [WELDED] ERC-2981. An ask, not a collection

# ⚠ [WELDED] THE THREE FREE-DOOR CAPS — SPOKEN 2026-08-12, ONE DOOR.
#   ("we only have one door this one and i need like max amount of people LOL
#   just not dust" — SENTENCES.md row 499.) Door 1 takes the whole free float;
#   doors 2 and 3 are welded shut, and so is the PAID door, because the four
#   below sum to the entire supply: 8092 + 0 + 0 + 100 = 8192.
#   A cap of 0 welds a door that can NEVER mint: setDoorRoot still succeeds,
#   /api/seat still reads the door as open, and every claim reverts for the life
#   of the contract. That is the intended answer for doors 2 and 3.
#   ⚠ IT IS ALSO THE ANSWER FOR THE PAID DOOR, WHICH IS THE CONSEQUENCE MOST
#   EASILY MISSED: paid ceiling = SUPPLY - SNAPSHOT - PLAY - BUILD - TREASURY
#   = 0, so NO SEAT IS EVER SOLD and the mint raises nothing. Activation burns
#   go to 0xdEaD rather than to us, so royalties are the only inflow this
#   collection ever has. That is a decision, not an oversight — do not "fix" it
#   by trimming door 1 without a new sentence.
#   ⚠ Door 1's root is 7.0x OVERSUBSCRIBED and that is deliberate: 57,010
#   wallets against 8,092 seats, so the door is FIRST-COME. See §3 of
#   docs/launch/HIVE-LAUNCH.md before you build a root against a different cap.
#   The root itself is
#   0x815c949e3cc0978bbf8cab595423076984b367660ee42fe4829f720bdef635d5
#   and it is NOT a constructor argument — it goes in later, via setDoorRoot(1).
#   ⚠ RE-DERIVE IT off the tracked artifact before you post it, never off this
#   comment: snapshots/seat-door1.MAX.2026-08-12.merkle.json is the record (this
#   comment once carried the root of the reverted 57,003-wallet rebuild, and a
#   root pasted from here would have refused every proof the box serves).
SEAT_SNAPSHOT_CAP=8092          # door 1 — every holder above dust, 17 cohorts
SEAT_PLAY_CAP=0                 # door 2 — welded shut
SEAT_BUILD_CAP=0                # door 3 — welded shut

# ⚠ [WELDED] THE RESERVE WINDOW — SPOKEN 2026-08-13: **0. FREE FOREVER.**
#   Operator: *"it can just be free forever thats fine"*, superseding the
#   2026-08-12 sentence of 60 days from deploy. Unix seconds; `0` means the three
#   free doors NEVER expire. This was always a real answer — the script demands
#   the field precisely so that answer has to be typed rather than defaulted into
#   — and it is now the chosen one. **No date to compute on the broadcast day.**
#
#   ⚠ WHAT 0 ACTUALLY WELDS, because it is more than "the doors stay open".
#   `_reserveReleased()` returns false for the life of the contract, so the
#   reserve never rejoins the paid float. Combined with the caps above:
#     paid ceiling = 8192 - 8092 - 0 - 0 - 100 = 0, permanently.
#   So a door-1 seat nobody claims is a seat that can NEVER be minted by anyone,
#   through any door, at any price. The collection's real supply is however many
#   people actually walk through door 1, plus the 100 treasury.
#
#   That is a good property rather than a cost, and it is worth saying out loud
#   on the surface: supply can only shrink, and there is no mechanism by which
#   the team sells the remainder later. It is also 7.0x oversubscribed, so the
#   remainder is likely to be small.
SEAT_RESERVED_UNTIL=0

# ⚠ [WELDED] THE LADDER. Closed 2026-08-12 — do not edit without a new sentence.
#   Whole SCRY, cumulative; an upgrade pays the difference. Spacing is 1/3/6/12/20
#   and NOT 1/3/7/14/20, which makes tier 4 strictly dominated.
SEAT_TIER_COSTS="20000,60000,120000,240000,400000"
SEAT_TIER_WEIGHTS="100,160,220,275,333"

# ⚠ [WELDED] THE SEAL. ⭐ ALREADY DRAWN 2026-08-12 — DO NOT REGENERATE.
#   The salt lives at /data/apps/secrets/scry-seat-salt.env, which is inside
#   backup-secrets.sh's `*.env` glob (it was a .txt for an hour, outside every
#   backup that exists, for a secret with no way to regenerate it).
#   ⚠ IT IS THE ASCII HEX STRING THAT IS HASHED, NOT THE DECODED BYTES —
#   revealSalt checks sha256(bytes(salt)) == saltCommitment, so committing to
#   the decoded bytes welds a deck that can never be opened.
#   Recompute the commitment off the FILE before you broadcast, never off a
#   shell variable, and check it against the value below:
#     S=$(grep -o '[a-f0-9]\{64\}' /data/apps/secrets/scry-seat-salt.env | head -1)
#     printf %s "$S" | openssl dgst -sha256 -r | cut -d' ' -f1
#   Verified matching 2026-08-12. Lose the file and every seat stays sealed for
#   as long as the contract exists.
SEAT_SALT_COMMITMENT=0xa0c225530afb99a186b514149e0dcd8b28aaf5eef50873c62fbeae850ecedd7e

# ── ScrySeat: setters, and deliberately deferred ─────────────────────────────
# [SETTER] The paid door. NOT set at deploy and not in this file on purpose:
#   the collection deploys with every door shut so nothing can be minted during
#   the broadcast. Post it later with setPaidDoor(priceWei, priceScry).
#   ⚠ A price of 0 is SHUT, not free. buyWithEth requires paidPriceWei > 0.

# ── ScryCistern: the drop bar ────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Deploy it right after the seat and BEFORE the mint — its constructor needs
# only the seat address, and a mint page asking people to burn 20,000 SCRY
# toward a contract that does not exist is a weak ask.
CISTERN_SCRY=0xDa2a4b23459e9ca88183e990802be644AcA7C4B0
CISTERN_SEAT=                   # fill in from the ScrySeat deploy
# CISTERN_ROUTER=               # omit => every claim pays SCRY, no swap, no
                                # counterparty. The honest opening state.

# All three SPOKEN 2026-08-12. Re-derive before broadcasting — the tape moves:
#     python3 meter/cistern_sizing.py --lp-share <ours>
# [TIMELOCK] whole SCRY. Two things pull against each other and no value
#   satisfies both at a low fee rate: a tier-1 share must beat what a claim
#   costs, and the bar must fire often enough to be worth watching. 20M was
#   ~$357 and ~monthly at the 2026-08-12 tape. If SCRY has moved a lot, the
#   CADENCE has moved with it — re-run the sizing before you accept this.
#   ⚠ IT HAS. Re-measured 2026-08-13: SCRY $0.00001281 (down ~28%) against
#   $14.24/day of fees (up ~34%), so 20M now fires every ~18 DAYS, not ~30.
#   Left at 20M deliberately — it is a 3-day-timelock setter, the 30-day claim
#   window is longer than the gap so nobody is squeezed out, and a tier-1 holder
#   still clears the ~$0.25 claim cost. Say 18 days, or raise it to ~33M.
CISTERN_THRESHOLD=20000000
# [SETTER] max 500. Never 0 — if only we can be bothered to crank open(), the
#   timing is discretionary again in practice, which is the one thing invariant
#   9 is closed against. 500 hands a bot a revenue share for one cheap tx;
#   200 of a 20M pot is 400,000 SCRY (~$7.13), which a bot will race on a chain
#   where gas is negligible. Raise it instantly if nobody cranks.
CISTERN_TIP_BPS=200
# [SETTER] seconds, and snapshotted per round so a change cannot reach backwards.
#   The cheap one: nothing is lost either way, since an unclaimed remainder
#   recycles into the next pot and rounds never block each other. 30 days matches
#   the monthly cadence 20M implies, so a holder who checks monthly never misses.
CISTERN_ROUND_WINDOW=2592000

# ── the throwaway rehearsal ──────────────────────────────────────────────────
# RUNBOOK.md §4e. Same SHAPE, play money — the constructor enforces sublinearity,
# so a test collection then behaves like the real one.
#   SEAT_SUPPLY=64 SEAT_SNAPSHOT_CAP=8 SEAT_PLAY_CAP=8 SEAT_BUILD_CAP=8 \
#   SEAT_TREASURY_CAP=24 SEAT_BURN_BPS=5000 SEAT_RESERVED_UNTIL=0 \
#   SEAT_TIER_COSTS="1,3,6,12,20" SEAT_TIER_WEIGHTS="100,160,220,275,333"
